-- Dennis C. Gallagher / housing -- a Season 2 row already exists at 4; rewrite it IN PLACE.
UPDATE inform.politician_context SET reasoning = 'Blanked 2026-10-07. 🔴 THE ROW SAYS SO ITSELF: THIS CHAIR IS A DEFAULT, NOT A FINDING. Its own reasoning reaches chair 4 by conceding there is no evidence and then seating the middle anyway -- "...structure (H.3997 suburban infrastructure fund). Not on Act on Mass tracker. Moderate Democrat default....". 🔑 A CENTRE CHAIR IS A CLAIM, NOT A DEFAULT. Chair 3 is a substantive position shown to voters as this person''s view; it is not a way of saying "unknown". The record already has a way of saying unknown, and this is it: value 0, which reads as unanswered. 🔑 AND A NON-SPONSORSHIP IS NOT A POSITION. Several of these rows rest on the member NOT having co-sponsored a particular bill, or on not appearing in a third-party tracker. An absent signature is not a vote against; it is not evidence of anything. A YES endorses, a NO only rejects, and a blank signature line says nothing at all. The sources examined are kept below so the next reader does not re-derive this. This is a blank, not a deletion -- the chair may well be re-researchable, and that is an invitation.', sources = ARRAY['https://malegislature.gov/Legislators/Profile/DCG2/Bills']::text[], updated_at = now()
